{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 1',lv:'U',n:1,q:"Why does a graded profile reduce the spread of arrival times?",say:'Question one. Why does a graded profile reduce the spread of arrival times?',cues:{k:'Question one',q:'Why does a graded'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 1',lv:'U',n:1,q:"Why does a graded profile reduce the spread of arrival times?",say:'Rays far from the axis travel longer paths. But they run through lower-index glass, where light is faster. With alpha near two, the extra speed nearly cancels the extra length, so rays arrive together.',cues:{a1:'Rays far from',a1b:'But they run',a2:'With alpha near'},al:[["Rays far from the axis travel longer paths, but through lower-index glass, where light is faster.",'a1'],["With α ≈ 2 the extra speed nearly cancels the extra length: the rays arrive close together.",'a2']],vis:(c,u,b)=>{
 const yc=290,hc=100,x0=20,x1=560;
 return `<defs><linearGradient id="ofGrad3" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#EDF2FF"/><stop offset="0.5" stop-color="#91A7FF"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#EDF2FF"/></linearGradient></defs>
${g('pop',tk(c,'a1'),OF_fiber(x0,x1,yc,hc,18,'url(#ofGrad3)')+OF_T(x0,40,'core: n highest on the axis',{fs:22,fw:700,fill:OF_GREY})+OF_arrow(x0,yc,x1,yc,BLU,5)+OF_T(x0,76,'axial ray: short path, slower glass',{fs:22,fw:800,fill:BLU}))}
${g('pop',tk(c,'a1b'),OF_wave(x0,x1,yc,92,270,ORG,5)+OF_T(x0,112,'swinging ray: long path,',{fs:22,fw:800,fill:ORG})+OF_T(x0,140,'in faster, lower-n glass',{fs:22,fw:800,fill:ORG}))}
${g('pop',tk(c,'a2'),`<circle cx="${x1}" cy="${yc}" r="16" fill="none" stroke="${GRN}" stroke-width="5"/>`+OF_T(x1,460,'α ≈ 2: they arrive together',{fs:24,fw:800,a:'end',fill:GRN}))}`}},
{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 2',lv:'A',n:2,q:"A step-index fiber has n₁ = 1.50, n₂ = 1.48, a = 20 µm and λ = 0.85 µm. Find NA, V and the mode count.",say:`Question two. Step index: n one, one point five zero; n two, one point four eight; core radius twenty micrometers; wavelength zero point eight five. Find ${P('NA')}, V, and the mode count.`,cues:{k:'Question two',q:'Step index: n'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 2',lv:'A',n:2,q:"A step-index fiber has n₁ = 1.50, n₂ = 1.48, a = 20 µm and λ = 0.85 µm. Find NA, V and the mode count.",say:'The root of zero point zero five nine six gives zero point two four four one. V is one hundred forty-seven point eight times that: thirty-six point zero nine. So about six hundred fifty-one modes.',cues:{fk:'The root of',k1:'The root of',k2:'V is one',k2b:'thirty-six point',k3:'So about six'},calc:{f:['NA = √(n₁² − n₂²)','V = (2πa/λ)·NA,   M ≈ V²/2'],hint:'a and λ are both in µm.',fk:'fk',steps:[["NA","NA = √(2.2500 − 2.1904) = √0.0596 = 0.2441","k1"],["V",["V = (2π × 20 / 0.85) × 0.2441","V = 147.8 × 0.2441 = 36.09"],["k2","k2b"]],["Modes","M ≈ 36.09² / 2 = 1303 / 2 = 651","k3"]],live:[0,1,2]}},
{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 3',lv:'N',n:3,q:"Compare a step-index and a parabolic graded-index fiber with the same n₁, n₂, a and λ on ray path, mode count and pulse spreading.",say:'Question three. Compare step-index and parabolic graded-index fibers, otherwise alike, on ray path, mode count and pulse spreading.',cues:{k:'Question three',q:'Compare step-index and'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 3',lv:'N',n:3,q:"Compare a step-index and a parabolic graded-index fiber with the same n₁, n₂, a and λ on ray path, mode count and pulse spreading.",say:'Step index: zig-zag rays, V squared over two modes, and a large spread, as steep rays go further. Graded index: curved rays, half the modes, and far less spread, as long paths run in faster glass.',cues:{a1:'Step index: zig-zag',a2:'Graded index: curved'},al:[["Step: zig-zag rays, M ≈ V²/2, large spread: steep rays go further at the same speed.",'a1'],["Graded: curved rays, M ≈ V²/4 (half), much less spread: longer paths run in faster glass.",'a2']],vis:(c,u,b)=>{
 const pulse=(xc,y,s,col)=>OF_poly(OF_fn(xc-80,xc+80,x=>y-70*Math.exp(-((x-xc)*(x-xc))/(2*s*s)),80),col,4);
 return `${g('pop',tk(c,'a1'),OF_T(20,40,'step index',{fs:24,fw:800,fill:BLU})+OF_fiber(20,420,130,40,12)+OF_zig(20,420,130,40,14,BLU,4)+OF_L(450,190,610,190,'#ADB5BD',3)+pulse(530,188,34,BLU)+OF_T(530,226,'wide spread',{fs:22,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:BLU})+OF_T(20,226,'M ≈ V²/2',{fs:22,fw:800,fill:BLU}))}
${g('pop',tk(c,'a2'),OF_T(20,290,'graded index',{fs:24,fw:800,fill:ORG})+OF_fiber(20,420,380,40,12)+OF_wave(20,420,380,32,140,ORG,4)+OF_L(450,440,610,440,'#ADB5BD',3)+pulse(530,438,11,ORG)+OF_T(530,476,'small spread',{fs:22,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:ORG})+OF_T(20,476,'M ≈ V²/4',{fs:22,fw:800,fill:ORG}))}`}},
{s:LS,k:'figs',term:'Your notes',title:'For your notes',say:'Your free notes are the PDF in the description. Redraw the two profiles, the V curve, and a pulse in its envelope.',cues:{t:'Your free notes',f:'Redraw the two'},tags:[["Free notes for this lesson (PDF)", "link in the description"], ["In this lesson", "Step-index and graded-index fibers; single-mode and multimode fibers and the cutoff wavelength; phase and group velocity"], ["Key terms and glossary", "at the end of the notes"]],figs:[["Step and graded index profiles", "n₁ = 1.48, n₂ = 1.46, a = 25 µm: the step drops at r = ±a; the parabola meets n₂ there, passing 1.4768 at 10 µm."], ["V against wavelength", "V = 2.765/λ for a = 4 µm, NA = 0.11: it crosses 2.405 at λ<tspan\tdy=\".28em\"\tfont-size=\".62em\">c</tspan><tspan\tdy=\"-.28em\">\u200b</tspan> = 1.15 µm; single-mode at 1.31 and 1.55 µm."], ["Carrier and envelope", "Crests slide forward through the envelope, which moves at v<tspan\tdy=\".28em\"\tfont-size=\".62em\">g</tspan><tspan\tdy=\"-.28em\">\u200b</tspan>; over 10 km the pulse lags the crests by 0.67 µs."]],note:"Sources your free notes draw on: Gerd Keiser (Optical Fiber Communications); John M. Senior (Optical Fiber Communications: Principles and Practice); Govind P. Agrawal (Fiber-Optic Communication Systems)"},
{s:OUT,k:'outro',term:'Outro',say:'So remember: grade the index to shrink the spread. Keep V below two point four zero five for one mode. Time every pulse with the group index. Next time, integrated optical waveguides. See you there!',cues:{f:'So remember',w1:'grade the index',w2:'Keep V below',w3:'Time every pulse',n:'Next time',s:'See you there'},words:[['GRADE THE INDEX','BLU','w1'],['V < 2.405: ONE MODE','ORG','w2'],['PULSES: GROUP INDEX','GRN','w3']],next:["NEXT TIME", "Next lesson", "Integrated optical waveguides", "book"],end:'See you there!'}
